ment: STM32 TIM3 makes a 6-cycle 1 MHz burst on two pins (second inverted = bridge drive, 6.6 Vpp) into transducer A; transducer B receives through U4/LNA/U7 into ADC1 at 4 MS/s (64 samples DMA). Then roles swap. 1000 up/down pairs per measurement." (at 20 280 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 34784ae6-34ba-47d0-ad85-df79a3a2618f)) (text "While receiving, one leg of the transducer is held low by its timer pin and the other is high-impedance and feeds the clamp + mux. LNA1 x10.2 (20 dB), LNA2 x10 (+20 dB), U7 selects 20 or 40 dB." (at 20 287 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid d016300c-3c25-406b-a653-c56398ec7bca)) (text "2-layer prototype. Production should use 4 layers (solid analog ground, guarded receive trace) - see docs." (at 20 294 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 5e700b7a-b4a4-4997-940b-c01489a49e00)) (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))))